  "post": {
    "caption": "This quartz is two gems in one. Ametrine is a quartz crystal with purple and gold zones, and its name combines amethyst and citrine. Iron in the crystal gives each zone its color, and cut stones often show an even split between the two colors. It has a hardness of seven on the Mohs scale, and commercial natural ametrine comes only from Bolivia's Anahí mine. Legend says a Spanish conquistador got the mine as a princess's dowry, and he reportedly gave its stones to the Spanish crown. The mine was rediscovered in the 1960s, and ametrine returned to the market in the 1970s.",
